lisa-design:
- Reply first, then chat.update the card. A failed edit returns *CardError together with the next state; cmd/notify logs ::warning:: and SAVES the state, because the reply is the notification and not saving would re-post it on the next run. A deleted/uneditable card must never block replies.
- Incident state gains additive fields (opened_sha, opened_at, again, resolved_at); a state saved before cards loads fine and its card falls back to the last SHA and no times. FailedJobs is now kept on recovery (for the struck-through list); dedupe only compares while Open, so this changes no transition.
- The needs-human CI field reflects the run's original result (before Route strips a release-checks-only failure), so the card says why release-checks blocked it.
- notify.Slack is kept (vuln-summary, attention-digest and train still post plain text) but delegates to slackkit.Client: one HTTP client for Slack. Its unused HTTP field was dropped.
- The closed-PR updates (needs-human card -> Handled, open incident -> Closed) come in the next PR of the stack; this one keeps the merged closed-PR guard unchanged.

